{
  "name": "Song Bench",
  "icon": "tribalpower:song_bench",
  "order": 70,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:song_bench",
      "text": [
        "The lattice's all-rounder. Seat one Echo-stage item and the bench sings it up the lattice, stage by stage, as long as each stage's voice is nearby.",
        "It costs far more Pulse than the dedicated stations, so use it for single items, not batches."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Singing",
      "text": [
        "Place the bench with its totems within 8 blocks. Right-click it with an Echo-stage item to seat it: stone for a shard (not cobble), an Echo Shard, an Attuned Echo or a Bound Echo. It holds one at a time.",
        "Click with an empty hand to sing. Crouch and click to take the item back.",
        "It keeps singing into the next stage whenever it can, and stops at a Manifested Ingot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What it costs",
      "text": [
        "- Shatter (Earth): **8 Pulse a tick** for 2 seconds.",
        "- Attune (Fire): **10 a tick** for 3 seconds.",
        "- Bind (Water): **12 a tick** for 4 seconds.",
        "- Manifest (Spirit): **16 a tick** for 5 seconds.",
        "The dedicated stations (Shatter, Attune, Bind, Manifest, Kiln, Unweave) use written recipes and cost much less.",
        "Ranking it in Echo Attune, Bind, then Manifest shortens the song; Pulse per tick rises and Pulse per craft stays about even."
      ]
    },
